Build a single-file retro arcade Snake game (`index.html`, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, no libraries) with a neon aesthetic. Press Start 2P font, dark background (#05050a), neon palette: green #39ff14, pink #ff2ec4, cyan #00f0ff, yellow #ffee00. A CRT scanline overlay (3px dark lines) covers the screen.

**Render modes:** 2D, 2.5D, and 3D, chosen by buttons labeled "2D / 2.5D / 3D" (no numeric prefixes) on the start screen, or by 1/2/3 keys at any time. Remember the last mode in localStorage. Switching into or out of 3D mid-run restarts the game. One persistent high score is shared across modes.

**Board sizes:**
- 2D and 2.5D: 20×20 grid, 24px cells, one layer.
- 3D: a roomy 14×14×14 volumetric cube. The snake moves in full 3D. Q/Space rises and E/Shift dives (real vertical moves). Walls include floor and ceiling.

**Controls:** Arrows/WASD move. In 3D, steering is camera-relative. Input buffers up to 2 queued moves and rejects 180° turns and duplicates. P toggles pause. Space/Enter starts from the start or game-over screens. Arrow/WASD also auto-starts.

**Speed:**
- 2D/2.5D: starts at 150ms per move, minus 4ms per food, floor 55ms.
- 3D: starts at 175ms, minus 3ms per food, floor 75ms. It is deliberately gentler than 2D.
- Yuzu slow-mo multiplies the interval by 1.8×.

**3D view:** Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom (zoom range 18–46). A gentle auto-orbit runs when not dragging. Draw a wireframe cyan cage with a glowing rim, a faint floor grid, and floor shadows. A pulsing ring marks the current layer. Show an elevation gauge on the right and a layer readout bottom-left. Segments scale and fade with distance. Show a brief control hint that fades after about 5 seconds.

**Vibybara conga theme:** The snake is a line of capybaras. The head has dark over-ear headphones (#1e0c0b) with yellow lightning bolts (#ffd23f). Bodies are light brown (#d58d59) with a darker muzzle (#5e3b2d) and dark ears (#2a1512). Body capys throw up a paw to the beat. Food is a pulsing pink yuzu with dimples, stem, and leaf. Death text is "THE CONGA STUMBLED".

**Power-ups:** Yuzu Berry slows time for 6s. Ghost Star lets the snake pass through itself for 6s. Each spawns every 6–13s, lasts 9s on the board, and blinks in the last 1.5s. Spawns land on free cells. Grabbing one emits 14 particles and shows a countdown badge (0.0s format) in the top center.

**Game states:** start, playing, paused, dying (650ms red/white flashing, descending sawtooth beep 220→140→80Hz, screen shake ±10px decaying over 420ms), and gameover. Eating plays an ascending beep. The start screen shows a pulsing title with "CONGA" in pink, mode buttons, and a blinking yellow "INSERT COIN" button. Game over shows the score, best score, and "NEW HI-SCORE" when earned, plus "PLAY AGAIN" (green) and "MAIN MENU" (cyan). M/Esc goes to the menu.
